 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value a JSON Pointer refers
+to. It throws an `Error` if the pointer is malformed (not empty and not starting with `/`, or a `~` not
+followed by `0` or `1`) or does not resolve (missing member, array index that is out of range, has leading
+zeros or is `-`, or descent into a primitive). Only own members of objects resolve.
