+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`: it
+returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws an error when the pointer is not a valid JSON
+Pointer or does not resolve to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- "" refers to the whole document; each `/token` descends one level.
+- `~1` decodes to `/`, `~0` to `~` (in that order); a bare `~` or `~` followed by another character is invalid.
+- A non-empty pointer not starting with `/` is invalid.
+- Array indices: `0` or digits without leading zeros; `-` (nonexistent element), leading zeros, signs and non-digits do not resolve.
+- Missing object members and descent into primitives or null throw; only own properties resolve.
+- Tests in `src/index.test.ts` cover happy and error paths (`npm test`).
